# Gitleaks exceptions
#
# Format:
# commit:file:rule:line
#
# The fingerprint is printed by gitleaks for each finding.
#
# Add an entry only when the finding is a confirmed false positive.
# Every exception must be documented with the reason above it, for example:
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# path/to/file.yml
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The value was an example placeholder, not a real secret.
# It was replaced in the following commit, but remains in the Git history.
#
# <commit-sha>:path/to/file.yml:<rule-id>:<line>
